 ## Stradella Chord Finder diagram notes
 
-The **Show realization explanation below diagram** master checkbox controls four subordinate options: **Harmonic identity**, **Pitch-class realization**, **Physical realization**, and **Registral voicing**. These controls appear only while the master option is enabled; turning it off keeps the previous selections. The lines appear below the diagram and in SVG/PNG exports, with left-aligned text and bold level labels. Registral voicing directly shows an ascending list of nominal pitches and their octaves (including unison multipliers such as `C3 ×2`), rather than a single lowest-note label. Chord-button-only construction is stated in Physical realization, not Registral voicing. A help tooltip explains the difference between these concise notes and **More explanation**. When all four choices are disabled, the footer is omitted, including its otherwise reserved diagram space. These controls do not alter **More explanation**, the recommendation algorithm, playback, or file names.
-
-The nested **Show nominal note spacing** option requires the Registral voicing level to be active; disabling that level retains but temporarily disables the spacing selection. Registral voicing is always the last item in both the settings menu and the footer. When selected, its original note list is replaced by a compact, intrinsically sized chart alongside the heading. The chart follows the explanation font slider within a bounded type scale. It reserves separate space for alternating pitch labels and semitone numbers, expands particularly tight horizontal gaps as needed, uses the configured Stradella register model, is exported with the diagram, and highlights one-semitone gaps in red. The numerals—not the exact drawn segment lengths—identify the semitone distances. The spacing option remains off by default.
+**Show realization explanation below diagram** controls the four optional footer levels: **Harmonic identity**, **Pitch-class realization**, **Physical realization**, and **Registral voicing**. They appear in that order in the settings menu and in exported SVG/PNG diagrams. The level checkboxes appear when the master option is enabled; disabling it preserves their selections. All four levels are enabled by default, and hiding all four removes the footer and its reserved space.
+
+**Registral voicing** lists nominal modeled pitches and octaves (including `×2` for duplicated unisons) from the configured Stradella bass and chord registers. These values do not represent measured acoustic frequencies. The nested **Show nominal note spacing** option, off by default, substitutes an interval chart for the pitch list. It displays semitone differences between adjacent nominal pitches, marks one-semitone gaps red, and includes the chart in SVG/PNG exports. The diagram text-size control affects the chart within bounded font sizes. Its horizontal spacing can expand to avoid collisions, so the numerical intervals, rather than line lengths, indicate semitone distances. Hiding Registral voicing disables the nested control without changing its stored value. Neither option alters chord generation, harmonic interpretation, ranking, audio, or filenames.
 
 The import/export setting `stradellaNoteLevels` is an object with boolean fields `identity`, `pitchClasses`, `voicing`, and `physical`, all `true` by default. Older settings files omit this object and continue to show all four lines. A partially specified object defaults only its missing/invalid fields to `true`. The default settings file in `public/default-settings.json` contains the same keys.
 
